1
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:23,895
Thank you.
谢谢。

2
00:00:23,895 --> 00:00:24,343
Thank you.
谢谢。

3
00:00:24,343 --> 00:00:24,630
Thank you.
谢谢。

4
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:27,010
Thank you, Chris.
谢谢你，克里斯。

5
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:28,770
Thank you, Blanca.
谢谢你，布兰卡。

6
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,150
And thank you all for being here.
感谢大家来到这里。

7
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:47,310
We just took back Texas.
我们刚刚夺回了得克萨斯州！

8
00:00:48,470 --> 00:01:02,900
We just proved that all the money in the world is no match for the people of Texas.
我们刚刚证明，全世界的金钱，也敌不过得州人民的力量。

9
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:15,580
We just showed that a politics of division is no match for a politics of love.
我们刚刚证明，制造分裂的政治，敌不过以爱为本的政治。

10
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:27,300
And we just sent a message to every billionaire mega donor, every trillionaire mega donor.
我们也向每一位身家数十亿、乃至数万亿的巨额捐款人发出了信息。

11
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:40,280
Every corrupt defender of this broken political system in this state, in this country, power belongs to the people.
向这个州、这个国家里，维护这套失灵政治体制的每一个腐败之徒宣告：权力属于人民。

12
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:55,300
I'm reminded of that story from Scripture of a shepherd boy who goes up against a giant.
这让我想起《圣经》中那个牧羊少年对抗巨人的故事。

13
00:01:56,060 --> 00:02:00,120
For 40 days, Goliath teases and taunts.
整整四十天，歌利亚不断挑衅、嘲弄。

14
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:03,680
On the day of the fight, he shows up in full armor.
决战那天，他全副武装地出现。

15
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:08,100
He's carrying so many weapons he needs someone else to carry his shield.
他带着那么多武器，甚至得让别人替他拿盾牌。

16
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:12,840
In this race, we went up against our own Goliaths.
这场竞选中，我们也面对着自己的“歌利亚”。

17
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:24,300
The richest man in the world, the most powerful man in the world, and the entire Washington DC establishment.
世界上最富有的人、最有权势的人，以及整个华盛顿的建制势力。

18
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:30,800
David wasn't as big or as strong as Goliath.
大卫没有歌利亚那么高大、强壮。

19
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,460
He didn't have as many weapons, but he had hope.
他的武器也没那么多，但他怀有希望。

20
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:34,900
He had faith.
他心有信仰。

21
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:38,020
And he had a slingshot.
他还有一副弹弓。

22
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:42,200
You were my slingshot.
你们就是我的弹弓。

23
00:02:45,930 --> 00:02:49,370
The people of Texas were my slingshot.
得州人民，就是我的弹弓。

24
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:58,460
And tonight And tonight, we defeated Goliath.
而今晚，我们击败了歌利亚。

25
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:11,130
Scripture has taught me, my own life has taught me, always bet on the underdog.
《圣经》和我自己的人生都告诉我：永远要相信那些不被看好的人。

26
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:16,350
Before I was a politician, I was a public school teacher.
从政之前，我是一名公立学校教师。

27
00:03:16,350 --> 00:03:20,570
I taught language arts at Rhodes Middle School on the west side of San Antonio.
我曾在圣安东尼奥西区的罗兹中学教授语言文学。

28
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:26,250
And as I always say, teaching middle school is the best preparation for politics.
正如我常说的，教中学生，是从政最好的准备。

29
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:32,010
The west side is a beautiful, historic neighborhood.
西区是一个美丽、历史悠久的社区。

30
00:03:32,470 --> 00:03:35,930
It's also one of the poorest zip codes in the entire state of Texas.
它也是整个得州最贫困的地区之一。

31
00:03:35,930 --> 00:03:42,850
Every day, my students struggled heroically to overcome a rigged system.
我的学生每天都在勇敢地抗争，努力跨越被不公平制度设置的障碍。

32
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:45,330
My students weren't just kids.
我的学生不只是孩子。

33
00:03:45,570 --> 00:03:48,970
They were survivors, dreamers, fighters.
他们是顽强的生存者、追梦者、奋斗者。

34
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:52,230
I saw it in their eyes every day.
我每天都能从他们眼中看到这些。

35
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:58,030
This unshakable resolve, this unconquered spirit.
那种不可动摇的决心，那种不屈不挠的精神。

36
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:02,510
Growing up, I saw that same fight in my mother.
从小到大，我也在母亲身上看到过同样的斗志。

37
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:06,230
A preacher's daughter from Laredo who left home at 19.
她是拉雷多一位牧师的女儿，十九岁就离开了家。

38
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:22,570
She moved up to Austin and met my birth father, a 21-year-old high school dropout whose drinking problem sometimes led to violence.
她搬到奥斯汀，遇见了我的生父。他二十一岁，高中辍学，酗酒有时会引发暴力。

39
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:26,670
One night he became abusive again.
一天晚上，他再次施暴。

40
00:04:27,670 --> 00:04:33,190
But that night my mother's love rose to meet that abuse.
但那一晚，母亲以爱鼓起勇气，反抗了暴力。

41
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:37,410
She packed all our stuff into her little Ford Escort.
她把我们所有的东西装进她那辆小小的福特 Escort。

42
00:04:37,429 --> 00:04:40,110
She drove me to the hotel where she worked.
她开车带我来到自己工作的酒店。

43
00:04:40,290 --> 00:04:47,050
She begged the manager to let us stay in one of the rooms until we found this little apartment in East Austin.
她恳求经理让我们暂住一间客房，直到我们在东奥斯汀找到一间小公寓。

44
00:04:47,694 --> 00:04:51,570
There wasn't there wasn't room for a nursery.
公寓里腾不出一间婴儿房。

45
00:04:52,110 --> 00:04:54,770
So I slept in a crib in her closet.
所以，我睡在她衣橱里的婴儿床上。

46
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,670
And she was so proud of that closet.
她却为那个衣橱感到无比自豪。

47
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,790
She decorated it with pictures and toys.
她用照片和玩具装饰它。

48
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:03,250
No one was going to tell her it wasn't a nursery.
谁也别想告诉她，那不是一间婴儿房。

49
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:10,900
Always bet on the underdog.
永远要相信不被看好的人。

50
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:21,120
We were the underdogs in this race.
这场竞选中，我们就是不被看好的那一方。

51
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:26,200
We went up against nearly 40 years of doubt and disillusionment.
我们面对的是将近四十年的怀疑与失望。

52
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:33,320
We went up against more than $300 million, more than any Senate campaign in American history.
我们面对的是超过三亿美元的资金，比美国历史上任何参议员竞选都多。

53
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:40,600
We went up against all the negative ads, smear campaigns, foreign bots, and AI deep fakes that money can buy.
我们面对的是金钱买得到的一切：负面广告、抹黑攻势、境外机器人账号和 AI 深度伪造。

54
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:47,640
Those attacks were the final howls of a dying establishment.
那些攻击，是垂死的建制势力最后的哀嚎。

55
00:05:49,118 --> 00:06:02,100
The death rattle of a status quo that knows its days are numbered.
是一个自知时日无多的旧秩序发出的临终喘息。

56
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:06,600
They played dirty because they were desperate.
他们不择手段，因为他们已经走投无路。

57
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,400
But we never lost hope.
但我们从未失去希望。

58
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,320
We never lost faith.
我们从未失去信念。

59
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:16,160
And against big money and long odds, we took our power back.
面对巨额资金和悬殊的胜算，我们仍然夺回了自己的权力。

60
00:06:19,466 --> 00:06:25,600
Always, always bet on the underdog.
永远，永远要相信不被看好的人。

61
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:32,700
We built a movement unlike any this state has ever seen.
我们建立了这个州前所未见的一场运动。

62
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:41,120
We united Texans from all backgrounds and beliefs onto one team to take on this broken, corrupt political system.
我们把不同背景、不同信仰的得州人团结在一起，共同挑战这个失灵、腐败的政治体制。

63
00:06:41,695 --> 00:06:50,140
First-time voters, three-time Trump voters, working people from every corner of this state who are fed up and ready for change.
首次投票的人、三次投给特朗普的人，以及全州各地受够了现状、准备迎接改变的劳动者。

64
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:59,240
This win is for every underdog who's been counted out and left behind.
这场胜利，属于每一个被低估、被抛在身后的人。

65
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:10,200
This win is for every teacher and every nurse, for every farmer and every rancher, for every young person who's trying to buy a home,
属于每一位教师和护士、每一位农民和牧场主、每一个努力买房的年轻人，

66
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:14,440
For every parent who's trying to put food on the table.
也属于每一个为养家糊口而奔忙的父母。

67
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:25,660
This win is for every Texan who's ever wondered if anyone is listening.
这场胜利，属于每一个曾怀疑是否有人倾听自己的得州人。

68
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:27,460
I heard you.
我听见了你们。

69
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,240
We heard you.
我们听见了你们。

70
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:32,200
And tonight the world hears you.
而今晚，全世界都听见了你们。

71
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:48,360
To the Texans who supported this movement, I am humbled by your trust and I will work every day to be worthy of it.
对于支持这场运动的得州人，你们的信任让我深感谦卑；我会每天努力，不辜负这份信任。

72
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:53,620
And to the Texans who didn't vote for me, I will be your senator too.
对于没有投票给我的得州人，我也会是你们的参议员。

73
00:07:54,120 --> 00:08:01,490
I will always I will always serve you.
我会始终为你们服务。

74
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:03,950
I will always fight for you.
我会始终为你们而奋斗。

75
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:08,250
This win is not about the Democratic Party or Republican Party.
这场胜利，不只关乎民主党或共和党。

76
00:08:08,470 --> 00:08:10,030
It's much bigger than that.
它的意义远远超出党派。

77
00:08:10,610 --> 00:08:15,350
There is something broken in America.
美国有些东西出了问题。

78
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:17,870
Our economic system is broken.
我们的经济体制出了问题。

79
00:08:18,510 --> 00:08:20,410
Our political system is broken.
我们的政治体制出了问题。

80
00:08:20,910 --> 00:08:24,630
Even our relationships with each other feel broken.
甚至我们彼此之间的关系，也让人觉得破碎了。

81
00:08:25,450 --> 00:08:31,370
That's because that's because the most powerful people in the world want it that way.
这是因为，世界上最有权势的人，就希望事情变成这样。

82
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:37,630
My granddad was a Baptist preacher in South Texas.
我的外祖父是得州南部的一位浸礼会牧师。

83
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:45,670
And when I was little, he told me that we follow a barefoot rabbi who gave us two commandments.
小时候，他告诉我，我们追随的那位赤脚拉比，给了我们两条诫命。

84
00:08:46,710 --> 00:08:48,790
Love God and love neighbor.
爱上帝，爱邻人。

85
00:08:49,270 --> 00:08:57,090
Because there is no love of God without love of neighbor.
因为不爱邻人，就谈不上爱上帝。

86
00:08:58,416 --> 00:09:08,240
Every every single person bears the image of the sacred.
每一个人，都体现着神圣的形象。

87
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:11,600
Every single person is holy.
每一个人，都是神圣的。

88
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:15,420
Not just my neighbor who looks like me.
不只是那些长得像我的邻人。

89
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:18,740
Not just my neighbor who prays like me.
不只是那些和我一样祈祷的邻人。

90
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:21,580
Not just my neighbor who votes like me.
不只是那些和我投票选择相同的邻人。

91
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:25,200
I am called to love all of my neighbors the way I love myself.
我蒙召去爱所有邻人，就像爱自己一样。

92
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:36,570
Because despite our differences, we all want the same things.
因为尽管我们存在差异，我们想要的其实是同样的东西。

93
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:46,210
A safe neighborhood, a good job, a high quality, well-funded public school, and the ability to see a doctor when we need one.
安全的社区、好的工作、优质且经费充足的公立学校，以及有需要时能看得起病。

94
00:09:52,240 --> 00:10:02,060
But the billionaires who own the social media algorithms, who own the cable news networks, who own the politicians fighting on our screens,
但那些控制社交媒体算法、有线新闻网络，以及屏幕上互相争吵的政客的亿万富翁，

95
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:04,540
They want us at each other's throats.
他们想让我们彼此撕咬。

96
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:09,900
They want us focused on how we're different instead of on how we're the same.
他们想让我们只盯着彼此的不同，而忽略我们的共同之处。

97
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:15,420
They want us looking left and right at each other instead of looking up at them.
他们想让我们左右互斗，而不抬头看看上面的他们。

98
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:20,280
The real fight in this country is not left versus right.
这个国家真正的对抗，不是左派对右派。

99
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,220
It is top versus bottom.
而是上层对下层。

100
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:40,880
The people at the top work so hard to keep us angry and divided because our unity is a threat to their wealth and their power.
顶层的人竭力让我们愤怒、分裂，因为我们的团结，会威胁他们的财富和权力。

101
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:44,000
We saw it in this race.
我们在这场竞选中看到了这一点。

102
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,700
We saw it in every billionaire funded attack ad.
我们在每一条由亿万富翁出资的攻击广告中，都看到了这一点。

103
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:57,880
The people at the top divide us by party, by race, by gender, by religion, by culture, so we don't notice that they are picking our pockets,
顶层的人以党派、种族、性别、宗教、文化划分我们，好让我们察觉不到，他们正在掏空我们的口袋，

104
00:10:57,880 --> 00:11:06,920
That they are defunding our schools, that they are gutting our healthcare, that they are raising taxes on all of us while they cut taxes for themselves.
削减学校经费、掏空医疗保障，给我们所有人加税，却给自己减税。

105
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:12,680
It is the oldest strategy in the world, divide and conquer.
这是世上最古老的策略：分而治之。

106
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:20,300
But tonight we sent a crystal clear message to the people at the top, we will not be conquered.
但今晚，我们向顶层的人发出了清楚无误的信息：我们不会屈服。

107
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:36,190
It I think it's safe to say that we are tired of being pitted against each other.
我想可以肯定地说，我们厌倦了被煽动着彼此对立。

108
00:11:36,650 --> 00:11:40,130
We are tired of being told to hate each other.
我们厌倦了被告知应该互相仇恨。

109
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:50,450
It has been 10 years of this kind of politics, politics as blood sport, politics as trolling and owning,
这种政治已经持续十年：把政治当作血腥竞技、当作挑衅和羞辱对手的游戏，

110
00:11:50,690 --> 00:11:52,870
Politics as professional wrestling.
当作职业摔跤表演。

111
00:11:53,410 --> 00:11:55,010
It tears families apart.
它撕裂家庭。

112
00:11:55,010 --> 00:12:00,390
It ends friendships and it leaves us all feeling terrible all the time.
它终结友谊，让我们所有人始终感到痛苦。

113
00:12:01,010 --> 00:12:08,990
People across the political spectrum are hungry for a different kind of politics, not a politics of hate,
不同政治立场的人，都渴望一种不同的政治：不是仇恨的政治，

114
00:12:10,170 --> 00:12:16,690
Not a politics of fear, not a politics of division, but a politics of love.
不是恐惧的政治，不是分裂的政治，而是爱的政治。

115
00:12:20,830 --> 00:12:30,300
My faith teaches me that love is the strongest force in the universe.
我的信仰告诉我，爱是宇宙中最强大的力量。

116
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,760
Love is not passive.
爱不是消极被动。

117
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,840
Love is not neutral.
爱不是无动于衷。

118
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:37,520
Love is not weak.
爱不是软弱。

119
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:42,960
Love requires that we stand between the bullies and the bullied.
爱要求我们站在霸凌者和受欺凌者之间。

120
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:47,800
Love requires that we look evil in the eye and not blink.
爱要求我们直视邪恶，毫不退缩。

121
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:53,340
That kind of love has always been a threat to the powers that be.
这样的爱，一直是当权者眼中的威胁。

122
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:56,500
That kind of love is revolutionary.
这样的爱，具有革命性的力量。

123
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:59,620
That kind of love is creative.
这样的爱，具有创造性的力量。

124
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,200
Hate is predictable.
仇恨总是千篇一律。

125
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,480
Hate is boring.
仇恨很无聊。

126
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:07,680
Hate can't lower our energy bills.
仇恨不能降低我们的能源账单。

127
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:11,100
Hate can't teach a child to read.
仇恨不能教会一个孩子阅读。

128
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,020
Hate can't build a future.
仇恨不能创造未来。

129
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:17,520
But what hate can't do love can.
但仇恨做不到的，爱可以做到。

130
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:27,810
Love can turn a student into a scholar.
爱能把学生培养成学者。

131
00:13:28,830 --> 00:13:31,870
Love can turn a closet into a nursery.
爱能把衣橱变成婴儿房。

132
00:13:32,870 --> 00:13:35,910
Love can turn an enemy into a friend.
爱能把敌人变成朋友。

133
00:13:36,790 --> 00:13:39,870
Love can turn a campaign into a movement.
爱能把一场竞选变成一场社会运动。

134
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:47,650
Love can heal what's broken in America.
爱能修复美国破碎的地方。

135
00:13:48,950 --> 00:13:53,730
We can't defeat the politics of division with more division.
我们不能用更多的分裂，击败制造分裂的政治。

136
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:55,190
We can't win that game.
那样的游戏，我们赢不了。

137
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:57,430
We have to change the game.
我们必须改变游戏规则。

138
00:13:58,210 --> 00:14:06,470
In my experience, when you extend an open hand rather than a closed fist, you'll be surprised by who takes that hand.
我的经验是，当你伸出友善的手，而不是挥起紧握的拳头，你会惊讶于谁会握住你的手。

139
00:14:07,270 --> 00:14:14,970
We didn't win this race by alienating our neighbors or shaming our neighbors or ridiculing our neighbors.
我们赢下这场竞选，并不靠疏远、羞辱或嘲弄邻人。

140
00:14:15,150 --> 00:14:23,830
We embodied a new kind of politics, a politics rooted in a deep love for our state, for our country,
我们践行了一种新的政治，根植于对我们的州、我们的国家，

141
00:14:23,950 --> 00:14:26,850
And most importantly, for all of our neighbors.
以及最重要的，对所有邻人的深厚热爱。

142
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:35,791
We mobilized.
我们动员了起来。

143
00:14:35,801 --> 00:14:43,991
We mobilized our 60,000 volunteers in every corner of this state, and together we delivered bottled water to Sandbranch,
我们动员全州六万名志愿者，一起把瓶装水送到桑德布兰奇，

144
00:14:44,450 --> 00:14:47,090
A community south of Dallas with no running water.
那是达拉斯以南一个没有自来水的社区。

145
00:14:48,050 --> 00:14:54,450
We donated school supplies to an elementary school in El Cenizo, a small town on the border.
我们向边境小镇埃尔塞尼索的一所小学捐赠了学习用品。

146
00:14:54,950 --> 00:15:02,250
We collected more than 20,000 lb of groceries for families in Fort Worth who are struggling under the high cost of living.
我们募集了两万多磅食品，送给沃思堡那些承受高昂生活成本的家庭。

147
00:15:02,890 --> 00:15:12,730
Before the world changes in ways you see on TV or read about in newspapers, the world changes person to person,
在世界出现那些你在电视上看到、在报纸上读到的变化之前，改变先发生在人与人之间，

148
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:14,730
Neighbor to neighbor.
邻里之间。

149
00:15:15,310 --> 00:15:25,870
In each moment when you choose to be kind, in each neighbor we choose to love, in each prayer that we say for someone who would not pray for us in return.
发生在你选择善良的每一刻，发生在我们选择去爱的每一位邻人身上，也发生在我们为那些不会回报祈祷的人所作的祈祷中。

150
00:15:26,810 --> 00:15:29,350
This is how we won Texas.
我们就是这样赢下得州的。

151
00:15:30,310 --> 00:15:33,530
This is a win the size of Texas.
这是一场和得州一样宏大的胜利。

152
00:15:33,530 --> 00:15:46,140
And now we have a mandate the size of Texas.
而现在，我们也肩负着和得州一样宏大的民意授权。

153
00:15:51,770 --> 00:15:57,890
This election was about chasing a vision of what this state can be.
这场选举，是为了追寻这个州本应成为的样子。

154
00:15:58,430 --> 00:16:06,830
Texas public schools that are the envy of the nation, a Texas economy that is second to none,
让得州的公立学校成为全国典范，让得州的经济首屈一指，

155
00:16:06,830 --> 00:16:11,610
And Texas families that are stronger and healthier than they've ever been before.
让得州的家庭比以往任何时候都更强健、更健康。

156
00:16:11,610 --> 00:16:18,510
It won't it won't happen overnight, but a giant state deserves giant dreams.
这不会一夜实现，但一个伟大的州，值得拥有宏大的梦想。

157
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:25,520
And we know how to get there.
而我们知道如何实现它。

158
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:34,220
We must get big money out of our politics so no billionaire or trillionaire can buy our elections.
我们必须让大金主退出政治，让任何亿万富翁、万亿富翁都无法收买我们的选举。

159
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:44,070
We must unrig this economic system that only benefits the top 1%.
我们必须改变这个只让最富有的百分之一受益的经济体制。

160
00:16:44,830 --> 00:16:51,510
We must pass universal healthcare so no one goes bankrupt just because they get sick.
我们必须通过全民医疗保障，让任何人都不再仅仅因为生病就破产。

161
00:16:51,930 --> 00:17:02,370
We must invest in our teachers and our students so every underdog has a fighting chance.
我们必须投资教师和学生，让每一个处于弱势的人都有公平竞争的机会。

162
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:13,780
We must end these corrupt forever wars that are driving up prices and killing our brave men and women in uniform.
我们必须结束这些腐败、无休无止的战争；它们抬高物价，夺去英勇军人的生命。

163
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:26,340
And we must heal the deep spiritual corruption at the root of all of these crises.
我们必须医治所有这些危机根源处，那种深层的精神腐败。

164
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:33,980
We must bridge the divides between us and repair the ties that bind us.
我们必须弥合分歧，修复将我们联系在一起的纽带。

165
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:42,460
We forged a new kind of politics here in the Lone Star State, an answer to this decade of division.
我们在孤星州开创了一种新的政治，回应这十年来的分裂。

166
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:50,320
We showed that when working people come together across every dividing line we can do extraordinary things.
我们证明了，劳动者跨越所有分界团结起来，就能做出非凡的事情。

167
00:17:50,320 --> 00:18:02,192
We won this race because people who are desperate for change now are going to get change.
我们赢下这场竞选；那些迫切渴望改变的人，如今将迎来改变。

168
00:18:02,210 --> 00:18:14,670
That old politics is dying and a new politics is being born through each of us, through every underdog,
旧的政治正在消亡，新的政治正在我们每一个人、每一个不被看好的人身上诞生，

169
00:18:15,030 --> 00:18:22,010
Through every David against every Goliath, through every Texan who believed in our state and believed in this movement.
诞生于每一个对抗歌利亚的大卫，诞生于每一个相信这个州、相信这场运动的得州人。

170
00:18:22,450 --> 00:18:23,970
Now the real work begins.
现在，真正的工作开始了。

171
00:18:24,903 --> 00:18:33,810
2,000 years ago, when the people at the top hurt his neighbors, that barefoot rabbi didn't stay in his room and pray.
两千年前，当权势者伤害他的邻人时，那位赤脚拉比没有只留在房里祈祷。

172
00:18:34,470 --> 00:18:47,293
He walked into the seat of power and he flipped over the tables of injustice.
他走进权力中心，掀翻了不公义的桌子。

173
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:56,540
As this movement heads to the seat of power, as we head to the United States Senate, we know what this moment requires of us.
当这场运动走向权力中心，当我们走进美国参议院，我们知道这个时刻要求我们做什么。

174
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,740
Texas, it's time to start flipping tables.
得州，是时候开始掀翻那些桌子了。

175
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,840
Thank you for being here.
感谢你们来到这里。